    "title": "Interpret interpersonal reference",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk6-reference-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Interpret interpersonal reference",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "This conversational pronoun can refer to another person or group, or sometimes to the speaker. Identify its referent from context; it can express respect, distance, complaint or an intimate tone. 人家 can be a playful or plaintive self-reference in intimate informal interaction. It is not a neutral substitute for 我 in formal or unfamiliar relationships.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "客人从很远的地方来，人家也需要休息。",
                "pinyin": "kèrén cóng hěn yuǎn de dìfang lái ， rénjia yě xūyào xiūxi 。",
                "meaning": "The guests have come a long way; they need rest too.",
                "audio": "5d6fdadf411fefeb9778b026eb104db50c3ef5abd0088e79cd021c63dcad4526"
              },
              {
                "text": "人家已经等了很久了。",
                "pinyin": "rénjia yǐjīng děng le hěn jiǔ le 。",
                "meaning": "I have already been waiting a long time. Said plaintively to an intimate companion.",
                "audio": "2fe9a8be943ac326da2a204b64fe7922276a20e4b36b8151475ce4dd91b5e44a"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "人家",
                "pinyin": "rénjia",
                "meaning": "other people; somebody else; I/me in context-dependent conversational self-reference",
